==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Great [[combo]] potential.
* Very big hitbox compared to other [[swords]].
* Good range.
* On the fourth swing, it provides a dash good for locomotion.
* Very good as a support weapon, as '''[X] Water Dragon Shower''' has a lot of [[AoE]] and a good [[stun]].

|'''[Z] Sea Dragon Fury'''
* Decent [[AoE]] damage, making it quite easy to hit.
* High knockback, which is useful against transformed [[Buddha]] users in [[PvP]].

|'''[X] Water Dragon Shower'''
* Does not require a lot of aiming.
* Largest [[Area of Effect|AoE]] in the game out of every [[Swords|sword]].
* Good stun.
* Brings down enemies to the ground, can be extremely viable against sky campers.
* [[Instinct/Break|Breaks Instinct]] if the player aims the center whirlpool at the enemy.
* Good for starting combos.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Melee attacks cause a short dash on the fourth swing, making it less ideal for auto clicking.
* High mastery requirements compared to most {{Rare}} [[swords]].
* No mobility.
* Low damage.

|'''[Z] Sea Dragon Fury'''
* High knockback can make it bad for grinding.
* Only [[Instinct/Break|breaks Instinct]] if aimed correctly.

|'''[X] Water Dragon Shower'''
* A bit weak in the air. (Can not hit players in the air if too close.)
* Can be dodged with [[Instinct]] if the target is at the end of the move.
* Useless in the [[water]]. (The shower goes beneath the sea.)
* Very low damage.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* If the player uses the Dragon Trident's [M1] dash attack in mid-air, they will go very far.
* The [[Tide Keeper]] uses the old abilities of Dragon Trident.
* The Dragon Trident is the only {{Rare}} [[Swords|sword]] to have its [X] move [[mastery]] requirement being 350.
* The Dragon Trident can be considered as an upgrade to the [[Trident]].

